    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1427">

                <pb facs="1795" n="1595" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1595"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/7–3045</note>
                <head>No. 1427<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Text Submitted by the British
                        Delegation</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1427-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-30">Undated</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Austria</hi></p>
                <p>The Conference examined a proposal by the Soviet Government on the extension of
                    the authority of the Austrian Provisional Government to all of Austria.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d1427-f2"/></p>
                <p>The three Governments agreed that they were prepared to examine this question
                    after the entry of the British and American forces into the city of Vienna.</p>
                <pb facs="1796" n="1596" xml:id="pg1596"/>
                <p>The Conference took note of a statement by Generalissimo Stalin that Marshal Koniev would continue to issue rations to the people of Vienna
                    until the British and American authorities were able to undertake the
                        task.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1427-f3"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1427-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1427-f1-content">
                <p>This draft text constitutes the fifth part of a third draft of the Protocol
                    prepared by the British Delegation, which bears the following notation:
                    “Compared with U. S. Text and agreed 30.7.45.” It was discussed at the Eleventh
                    Meeting of the Foreign Ministers, August 1. See <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg553">p. 553</ref>. Cf. <ref target="#d1428"
                        >document No. 1428</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1427-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1427-f2-content">
                <p>See <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg311">p. 311</ref>.</p>
            </note>
